@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `bvvcx-nouns`
IMPORT `bvvcx-p1-definitions`
IMPORT `bvvcx-p2-contract`
IMPORT `bvvcx-p2-duties`
IMPORT `bvvcx-p2-claims`
IMPORT `bvvcx-tests-fixtures`

-- Tests for Part I and Part II. Every expected value was worked by hand from the quoted
-- source lines before it was written here; the calendar arithmetic was checked with a
-- calendar, not with the L4 library. The fixtures are in bvvcx-tests-fixtures.l4.

§ `Tests — Part I definitions`

-- Definition 14: a car, not a motorcycle.
#ASSERT `a car within definition 14` `the standard vehicle`
#ASSERT NOT `a car within definition 14` `a two-wheeled motorcycle`

-- Definition 12: January 2022 to January 2026 is 48 months; with no registration month, from
-- June of the year of manufacture: June 2020 to January 2026 is 67 months.
#ASSERT `the time in use, in months, when the insurance began, of` `the standard vehicle` `under` `the standard policy` EQUALS 48
#ASSERT `the time in use, in months, when the insurance began, of` (`a used car worth 600 million, registered` NOTHING `, made in` 2020) `under` `the standard policy` EQUALS 67
#ASSERT `the time in use, in months, when the insurance began, of` (`a used car worth 600 million, registered` (`registered in` 2023 `,` 2) `, made in` 2022) `under` `the standard policy` EQUALS 35

-- Definition 8: the driver drives with consent.
#ASSERT `the driver within definition 8` `a sober licensed driver with consent`
#ASSERT NOT `the driver within definition 8` (`a person driving: consent` FALSE `, licence` TRUE `, expired` FALSE `, right class` TRUE `, withdrawn` FALSE `, learner` FALSE `, blood` NOTHING `, breath` NOTHING `, drugs` FALSE `, refused a test` FALSE)

-- Definition 2: an owner, or a lawful holder by the owner's hand-over, who concluded and paid.
`a borrower who concluded and paid` MEANS `The purchaser` WITH
    `owns the vehicle`                                                     IS FALSE
    `holds or uses the vehicle lawfully, the owner having handed it over`  IS TRUE
    `concluded the contract with the insurer`                              IS TRUE
    `paid the premium in full`                                             IS TRUE
`an owner who has not paid in full` MEANS `The purchaser` WITH
    `owns the vehicle`                                                     IS TRUE
    `holds or uses the vehicle lawfully, the owner having handed it over`  IS FALSE
    `concluded the contract with the insurer`                              IS TRUE
    `paid the premium in full`                                             IS FALSE
#ASSERT `a purchaser within definition 2` `a borrower who concluded and paid`
#ASSERT NOT `a purchaser within definition 2` `an owner who has not paid in full`

-- Definitions 3 and 10: a physical explosion is not an explosion.
#ASSERT `a fire within definition 3` `a fire`
#ASSERT `an explosion within definition 10` `an explosion`
#ASSERT NOT `an explosion within definition 10` `a physical explosion from excess pressure`

§ `Tests — front matter and Article 1`

#ASSERT `the notice — the purchaser is taken to have understood the whole of the Rules` `the standard policy`
#ASSERT count `Article 1 — the documents that make up the contract` EQUALS 5
-- Signed: the 1.1 deeming does not arise. Unsigned but paid: it does.
#ASSERT NOT `1.1 — the requester is taken to agree with the information on the contract issued` `the standard policy`
`an unsigned but paid policy` MEANS `The policy` WITH
    `the date the contract was concluded`                     IS YMD 2025 12 28
    `the start of the period of insurance`                    IS YMD 2026 1 1
    `the end of the period of insurance`                      IS YMD 2026 12 31
    `the sum insured`                                         IS 600_000_000
    `the deductible stated on the certificate`                IS NOTHING
    `the certificate states reduction rates of its own`       IS FALSE
    `the supplementary clauses on the certificate`            IS EMPTY
    `a clause agreed under Article 23 is on the certificate`  IS FALSE
    `the car-hire sum insured per day`                        IS NOTHING
    `the car-hire sum insured per event`                      IS NOTHING
    `a contract for a group of vehicles`                      IS FALSE
    `the request form was signed or confirmed electronically` IS FALSE
    `the premium arrangements`                                IS `premium paid in full at conclusion`
    `a notice of unilateral termination`                      IS NOTHING
    `a transfer of ownership`                                 IS NOTHING
#ASSERT `1.1 — the requester is taken to agree with the information on the contract issued` `an unsigned but paid policy`

§ `Tests — Articles 2 and 3: the standing of the contract`

§§ `2.1 — the period`

-- 1 January to 31 December 2026, both days inside (fork F8).
#ASSERT `the standing of the contract on` (YMD 2026 1 1)   `for` `the insured named on the certificate` `under` `the standard policy` EQUALS `in effect`
#ASSERT `the standing of the contract on` (YMD 2026 12 31) `for` `the insured named on the certificate` `under` `the standard policy` EQUALS `in effect`
#ASSERT `the standing of the contract on` (YMD 2027 1 1)   `for` `the insured named on the certificate` `under` `the standard policy` EQUALS `outside the period of insurance (2.1)`
#ASSERT `the standing of the contract on` (YMD 2025 12 31) `for` `the insured named on the certificate` `under` `the standard policy` EQUALS `outside the period of insurance (2.1)`

§§ `2.2, 2.3, 3.1 — the premium`

GIVEN `the arrangements` IS A `The premium arrangements`
GIVETH A `The policy`
`the standard policy, but premium` `the arrangements` MEANS
    `a 2026 policy: sum insured` 600_000_000 `, deductible` NOTHING `, clauses` EMPTY `, ending` (YMD 2026 12 31)
        `, premium` `the arrangements` `, notice` NOTHING `, transfer` NOTHING

`unpaid, no agreement, due 1 January` MEANS
    `premium arrangements: written agreement` FALSE `, due` (YMD 2026 1 1) `, paid in full on` NOTHING `, continued from` NOTHING
`unpaid, payment agreed by 31 January` MEANS
    `premium arrangements: written agreement` TRUE `, due` (YMD 2026 1 31) `, paid in full on` NOTHING `, continued from` NOTHING
`paid on 25 January, payment agreed by 31 January` MEANS
    `premium arrangements: written agreement` TRUE `, due` (YMD 2026 1 31) `, paid in full on` (JUST (YMD 2026 1 25)) `, continued from` NOTHING
`paid late on 10 February, payment agreed by 31 January` MEANS
    `premium arrangements: written agreement` TRUE `, due` (YMD 2026 1 31) `, paid in full on` (JUST (YMD 2026 2 10)) `, continued from` NOTHING
`paid late, continued from 1 March` MEANS
    `premium arrangements: written agreement` TRUE `, due` (YMD 2026 1 31) `, paid in full on` (JUST (YMD 2026 2 10)) `, continued from` (JUST (YMD 2026 3 1))

-- No agreement on time, nothing paid: not in effect on the first day (2.2); ended from the
-- day after the due date (2.3, 3.1.1).
#ASSERT `3.1.1 — the date the contract ends for non-payment under` `unpaid, no agreement, due 1 January` EQUALS JUST (YMD 2026 1 2)
#ASSERT `the standing of the contract on` (YMD 2026 1 1) `for` `the insured named on the certificate` `under` (`the standard policy, but premium` `unpaid, no agreement, due 1 January`) EQUALS `not in effect, the premium not having been paid (2.2)`
#ASSERT `the standing of the contract on` (YMD 2026 1 5) `for` `the insured named on the certificate` `under` (`the standard policy, but premium` `unpaid, no agreement, due 1 January`) EQUALS `ended for non-payment of the premium (2.3, 3.1.1)`
-- A written agreement to pay by 31 January: in effect up to and including 31 January.
#ASSERT `the standing of the contract on` (YMD 2026 1 20) `for` `the insured named on the certificate` `under` (`the standard policy, but premium` `unpaid, payment agreed by 31 January`) EQUALS `in effect`
#ASSERT `the standing of the contract on` (YMD 2026 1 31) `for` `the insured named on the certificate` `under` (`the standard policy, but premium` `unpaid, payment agreed by 31 January`) EQUALS `in effect`
#ASSERT `the standing of the contract on` (YMD 2026 2 1)  `for` `the insured named on the certificate` `under` (`the standard policy, but premium` `unpaid, payment agreed by 31 January`) EQUALS `ended for non-payment of the premium (2.3, 3.1.1)`
#ASSERT `the standing of the contract on` (YMD 2026 6 15) `for` `the insured named on the certificate` `under` (`the standard policy, but premium` `paid on 25 January, payment agreed by 31 January`) EQUALS `in effect`
-- Paid late: still ended, unless the insurer accepted continuation in writing (3.1.3).
#ASSERT `the standing of the contract on` (YMD 2026 6 15) `for` `the insured named on the certificate` `under` (`the standard policy, but premium` `paid late on 10 February, payment agreed by 31 January`) EQUALS `ended for non-payment of the premium (2.3, 3.1.1)`
#ASSERT `the standing of the contract on` (YMD 2026 2 15) `for` `the insured named on the certificate` `under` (`the standard policy, but premium` `paid late, continued from 1 March`) EQUALS `ended for non-payment of the premium (2.3, 3.1.1)`
#ASSERT `the standing of the contract on` (YMD 2026 3 1)  `for` `the insured named on the certificate` `under` (`the standard policy, but premium` `paid late, continued from 1 March`) EQUALS `in effect`

§§ `3.2.1 — a notice of unilateral termination`

GIVEN `the stated date` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A `The policy`
`the standard policy, with an insurer's notice of 20 June stating` `the stated date` MEANS
    `a 2026 policy: sum insured` 600_000_000 `, deductible` NOTHING `, clauses` EMPTY `, ending` (YMD 2026 12 31)
        `, premium` `premium paid in full at conclusion`
        `, notice` (JUST (`A notice of unilateral termination` WITH
                              `given by`                         IS `the insurer`
                              `date of the notice`               IS YMD 2026 6 20
                              `the termination date it states`   IS `the stated date`
                              `date the other party received it` IS YMD 2026 6 22))
        `, transfer` NOTHING

#ASSERT `the standing of the contract on` (YMD 2026 6 29) `for` `the insured named on the certificate` `under` (`the standard policy, with an insurer's notice of 20 June stating` (JUST (YMD 2026 6 30))) EQUALS `in effect`
#ASSERT `the standing of the contract on` (YMD 2026 6 30) `for` `the insured named on the certificate` `under` (`the standard policy, with an insurer's notice of 20 June stating` (JUST (YMD 2026 6 30))) EQUALS `ended by a notice of unilateral termination (3.2.1)`
-- No date stated: it ends on the date of the notice.
#ASSERT `the standing of the contract on` (YMD 2026 6 19) `for` `the insured named on the certificate` `under` (`the standard policy, with an insurer's notice of 20 June stating` NOTHING) EQUALS `in effect`
#ASSERT `the standing of the contract on` (YMD 2026 6 20) `for` `the insured named on the certificate` `under` (`the standard policy, with an insurer's notice of 20 June stating` NOTHING) EQUALS `ended by a notice of unilateral termination (3.2.1)`

§§ `2.4 — a transfer of ownership`

GIVEN `asked to end` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `The policy`
`the standard policy, the vehicle transferred on 1 May, the former owner asking to end it:` `asked to end` MEANS
    `a 2026 policy: sum insured` 600_000_000 `, deductible` NOTHING `, clauses` EMPTY `, ending` (YMD 2026 12 31)
        `, premium` `premium paid in full at conclusion` `, notice` NOTHING
        `, transfer` (JUST (`A transfer of ownership` WITH `date of the transfer` IS YMD 2026 5 1, `the former owner asked to end the contract` IS `asked to end`))

#ASSERT `the standing of the contract on` (YMD 2026 6 15) `for` `a new owner to whom the vehicle was transferred` `under` (`the standard policy, the vehicle transferred on 1 May, the former owner asking to end it:` FALSE) EQUALS `in effect`
#ASSERT `the standing of the contract on` (YMD 2026 6 15) `for` `the insured named on the certificate` `under` (`the standard policy, the vehicle transferred on 1 May, the former owner asking to end it:` FALSE) EQUALS `ended for the former owner when the vehicle was transferred (2.4)`
#ASSERT `the standing of the contract on` (YMD 2026 4 15) `for` `a new owner to whom the vehicle was transferred` `under` (`the standard policy, the vehicle transferred on 1 May, the former owner asking to end it:` FALSE) EQUALS `not in effect for a new owner before a transfer (2.4)`
#ASSERT `the standing of the contract on` (YMD 2026 4 15) `for` `the insured named on the certificate` `under` (`the standard policy, the vehicle transferred on 1 May, the former owner asking to end it:` FALSE) EQUALS `in effect`
#ASSERT `the standing of the contract on` (YMD 2026 6 15) `for` `a new owner to whom the vehicle was transferred` `under` (`the standard policy, the vehicle transferred on 1 May, the former owner asking to end it:` TRUE) EQUALS `ended at the former owner's request when the vehicle was transferred (2.4)`

§ `Tests — Article 3: refunds`

-- Premium 3,650,000 for 365 days. Ended on 2 July 2026: 183 days remain (2 July to
-- 31 December), worth 1,830,000. 70% of that is 1,281,000.
#ASSERT `3.2.2 — the refund of` 3_650_000 `when the purchaser ends the contract on` (YMD 2026 7 2) `under` `the standard policy` `, liability having arisen:` FALSE EQUALS 1_281_000
#ASSERT `3.2.2 — the refund of` 3_650_000 `when the purchaser ends the contract on` (YMD 2026 7 2) `under` `the standard policy` `, liability having arisen:` TRUE EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `3.2.4 — the refund of` 3_650_000 `when the insurer ends the contract on` (YMD 2026 7 2) `under` `the standard policy` EQUALS 1_830_000
-- 3.2.3: a group of two; the second vehicle has had a claim.
#ASSERT `3.2.3 — the refund on a group contract ended by the purchaser on` (YMD 2026 7 2) `under` `the standard policy` `for` (LIST (`A vehicle under a group contract` WITH `its premium` IS 3_650_000, `liability to compensate has arisen for it` IS FALSE), (`A vehicle under a group contract` WITH `its premium` IS 7_300_000, `liability to compensate has arisen for it` IS TRUE)) EQUALS 1_281_000
-- 3.1.2: ended on 2 January with nothing paid: the 1 day before the end earned 10,000, which
-- the insurer asks for. Paid in full and ended on 2 July: 182 days earned 1,820,000, so
-- 1,830,000 is refunded, or nothing once liability has arisen.
#ASSERT `3.1.2 — the premium the insurer asks for on an end on` (YMD 2026 1 2) `under` (`the standard policy, but premium` `unpaid, no agreement, due 1 January`) EQUALS 10_000
#ASSERT `3.1.2 — the premium to refund on an end on` (YMD 2026 1 2) `under` (`the standard policy, but premium` `unpaid, no agreement, due 1 January`) `, liability having arisen:` FALSE EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `3.1.2 — the premium to refund on an end on` (YMD 2026 7 2) `under` `the standard policy` `, liability having arisen:` FALSE EQUALS 1_830_000
#ASSERT `3.1.2 — the premium to refund on an end on` (YMD 2026 7 2) `under` `the standard policy` `, liability having arisen:` TRUE EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `3.1.2 — the premium the insurer asks for on an end on` (YMD 2026 7 2) `under` `the standard policy` EQUALS 0

§ `Tests — Articles 4 and 5: deadlines`

`a file the competent authority concluded on 10 May` MEANS `The claim file` WITH
    `date the complete and valid file was received`               IS YMD 2026 3 2
    `the insurer has to verify the file`                          IS TRUE
    `the insurer lacks authority to verify some element`          IS TRUE
    `date the insurer asked the competent authority to verify`    IS JUST (YMD 2026 3 10)
    `date of the competent authority's official conclusion`       IS JUST (YMD 2026 5 10)
`a file the competent authority has not concluded on` MEANS `The claim file` WITH
    `date the complete and valid file was received`               IS YMD 2026 3 2
    `the insurer has to verify the file`                          IS TRUE
    `the insurer lacks authority to verify some element`          IS TRUE
    `date the insurer asked the competent authority to verify`    IS JUST (YMD 2026 3 10)
    `date of the competent authority's official conclusion`       IS NOTHING

#ASSERT `4.2.3 — the last day for the insurer to pay on` `a file the competent authority concluded on 10 May` EQUALS YMD 2026 5 25
#ASSERT REFUSED `4.2.3 — the last day for the insurer to pay on` `a file the competent authority has not concluded on` BECAUSE "4.2.3 sets no time for paying a claim the competent authority has not concluded on"

-- Working days: Tuesday 6 October 2026 plus 5 working days is Tuesday 13 October; with
-- Thursday 8 October a holiday, Wednesday 14 October. Thursday 23 April 2026 plus 15
-- working days, with 30 April and 1 May holidays, is Monday 18 May.
#ASSERT `4.2.7 — the last day to reassess the risk after a notice received on` (YMD 2026 10 6) `, the public holidays being` (LIST (YMD 2026 10 8)) EQUALS YMD 2026 10 14
#ASSERT `5.2.4 — the last day to notify a change in risk made on` (YMD 2026 4 23) `, the public holidays being` (LIST (YMD 2026 4 30), (YMD 2026 5 1)) EQUALS YMD 2026 5 18
#ASSERT `a working day:` (YMD 2026 10 6) `, the public holidays being` EMPTY
#ASSERT NOT `a working day:` (YMD 2026 10 10) `, the public holidays being` EMPTY

-- 4.2.7: re-rating from 3,650,000 to 4,380,000 on 2 July: 730,000 x 183/365 = 366,000 more;
-- down to 2,920,000: 366,000 back.
#ASSERT `4.2.7 — the premium adjustment from` 3_650_000 `to` 4_380_000 `on a change on` (YMD 2026 7 2) `under` `the standard policy` EQUALS 366_000
#ASSERT `4.2.7 — the premium adjustment from` 3_650_000 `to` 2_920_000 `on a change on` (YMD 2026 7 2) `under` `the standard policy` EQUALS -366_000

-- The regulative rules, run against events (clocks: days unless the rule says hours).
#TRACE `4.2.3 — the insurer pays` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the insurer` DOES `pay the compensation` AT 15
#TRACE `4.2.3 — the insurer pays` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 16)
#TRACE `4.2.3 — the insurer pays` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the insurer` DOES `pay the compensation` AT 30
#TRACE `4.2.4 — the insurer gives its reasons for a refusal` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 16)
#TRACE `5.2.6(a) — the purchaser tells the insurer at once` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the purchaser` DOES `notify the insurer's customer-care hotline` AT 7
#TRACE `5.2.10 — the purchaser reports a theft of the vehicle within 24 hours` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the purchaser` DOES `notify the police and the insurer of the theft` AT 20
#TRACE `3.2.2 — the insurer refunds within 15 days of receiving the purchaser's notice` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the insurer` DOES `refund the premium for the rest of the period` AT 15

§ `Tests — Article 6: the cost of an independent assessment`

#ASSERT `6.3 — who pays for the independent assessment` (`The independent assessment` WITH `its conclusion differs from the insurer's` IS TRUE, `its cost` IS 5_000_000) EQUALS LIST `the insurer`
#ASSERT `6.3 — who pays for the independent assessment` (`The independent assessment` WITH `its conclusion differs from the insurer's` IS FALSE, `its cost` IS 5_000_000) EQUALS LIST `the insured`, `the driver`
#ASSERT count `6.2 — the courts that may appoint an independent assessor` EQUALS 2

§ `Tests — Article 7: the claim file`

GIVEN `police`     IS A BOOLEAN
      `third`      IS A BOOLEAN
      `stolen`     IS A BOOLEAN
      `criminal`   IS A BOOLEAN
      `lost`       IS A BOOLEAN
      `temporary`  IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `The circumstances of the claim`
`circumstances: police` `police` `, third party` `third` `, stolen whole` `stolen` `, criminal case` `criminal` `, papers lost` `lost` `, temporary circulation` `temporary` MEANS
    `The circumstances of the claim` WITH
        `the police took part in dealing with the accident`         IS `police`
        `a third party is liable for the damage`                    IS `third`
        `settled by mediation`                                      IS FALSE
        `a court judgment or decision`                              IS FALSE
        `the vehicle was sold, transferred, given or lent`          IS FALSE
        `the vehicle was stolen or robbed whole`                    IS `stolen`
        `a criminal case was opened`                                IS `criminal`
        `papers kept in the stolen vehicle were lost with it`       IS `lost`
        `circulating temporarily with the written approval of the competent authority` IS `temporary`
        `in the course of its first registration and inspection in Vietnam` IS FALSE

-- A collision the police dealt with, a third party at fault: 7.1.1, 7.1.2(a), (b), (d),
-- 7.1.3(a), (b), 7.1.6, 7.2.1(a)-(e), 7.2.2(a), (b), 7.2.3, 7.3 = 16 documents.
#ASSERT count (`Article 7 — the documents the claim file may contain, for` (`circumstances: police` TRUE `, third party` TRUE `, stolen whole` FALSE `, criminal case` FALSE `, papers lost` FALSE `, temporary circulation` FALSE)) EQUALS 16
-- A theft with a criminal case and lost papers: 7.1.1, 7.1.2(a), (b), (d), 7.3, 7.4.1-7.4.4 = 9.
#ASSERT count (`Article 7 — the documents the claim file may contain, for` (`circumstances: police` FALSE `, third party` FALSE `, stolen whole` TRUE `, criminal case` TRUE `, papers lost` TRUE `, temporary circulation` FALSE)) EQUALS 9
#ASSERT elem `7.4.3 the decision suspending the investigation or the prosecution` (`Article 7 — the documents the claim file may contain, for` (`circumstances: police` FALSE `, third party` FALSE `, stolen whole` TRUE `, criminal case` FALSE `, papers lost` FALSE `, temporary circulation` FALSE))
#ASSERT NOT elem `7.1.3(a) valid vouchers for the repair or replacement` (`Article 7 — the documents the claim file may contain, for` (`circumstances: police` FALSE `, third party` FALSE `, stolen whole` TRUE `, criminal case` FALSE `, papers lost` FALSE `, temporary circulation` FALSE))
-- 7.1.2(d): a vehicle circulating temporarily need not show an inspection certificate.
#ASSERT NOT elem `7.1.2(d) a valid inspection certificate` (`Article 7 — the documents the claim file may contain, for` (`circumstances: police` FALSE `, third party` FALSE `, stolen whole` FALSE `, criminal case` FALSE `, papers lost` FALSE `, temporary circulation` TRUE))
#ASSERT elem `7.1.2(d) a valid inspection certificate` (`Article 7 — the documents the claim file may contain, for` (`circumstances: police` FALSE `, third party` FALSE `, stolen whole` FALSE `, criminal case` FALSE `, papers lost` FALSE `, temporary circulation` FALSE))

§ `Tests — Article 8: double insurance`

-- Sum insured 600 million here and 400 million elsewhere on the same conditions: 600/1000.
#ASSERT `8.1 — this insurer's share of a loss, with sum insured` 600_000_000 `and other insurance` (LIST (`Another insurance of the vehicle` WITH `the sum insured under it` IS 400_000_000, `on the same conditions as this contract` IS TRUE)) EQUALS 0.6
-- Different conditions: each pays under its own contract (8.2).
#ASSERT `8.1 — this insurer's share of a loss, with sum insured` 600_000_000 `and other insurance` (LIST (`Another insurance of the vehicle` WITH `the sum insured under it` IS 400_000_000, `on the same conditions as this contract` IS FALSE)) EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `8.1 — this insurer's share of a loss, with sum insured` 600_000_000 `and other insurance` EMPTY EQUALS 1

§ `Tests — Article 9: time limits`

GIVEN `the claim date`  IS A DATE
      `the notice date` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the dispute`     IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A `The time limits of a claim`
`limits for a loss on 15 June 2026, claimed on` `the claim date` `, settlement notice received` `the notice date` `, dispute arising` `the dispute` MEANS
    `The time limits of a claim` WITH
        `date of the insured event`                                   IS YMD 2026 6 15
        `days lost to force majeure or other objective obstacles`     IS 0
        `date the claim was made`                                     IS `the claim date`
        `date the purchaser or the insured received the insurer's settlement notice` IS `the notice date`
        `days lost to illness, natural disaster, epidemic or other objective obstacles` IS 5
        `date the complaint was made`                                 IS NOTHING
        `date the dispute arose`                                      IS `the dispute`
        `date the suit was filed`                                     IS NOTHING

#ASSERT `9.1 — the claim was made in time` (`limits for a loss on 15 June 2026, claimed on` (YMD 2027 6 15) `, settlement notice received` NOTHING `, dispute arising` NOTHING)
#ASSERT NOT `9.1 — the claim was made in time` (`limits for a loss on 15 June 2026, claimed on` (YMD 2027 6 16) `, settlement notice received` NOTHING `, dispute arising` NOTHING)
-- 90 days from 1 August 2026 plus 5 days lost to illness: 4 November 2026.
#ASSERT `9.2 — the last day to complain about the settlement` (`limits for a loss on 15 June 2026, claimed on` (YMD 2026 7 1) `, settlement notice received` (JUST (YMD 2026 8 1)) `, dispute arising` NOTHING) EQUALS YMD 2026 11 4
#ASSERT REFUSED `9.2 — the last day to complain about the settlement` (`limits for a loss on 15 June 2026, claimed on` (YMD 2026 7 1) `, settlement notice received` NOTHING `, dispute arising` NOTHING) BECAUSE "the record does not say when the settlement notice was received"
#ASSERT REFUSED `9.3 — the last day to sue` (`limits for a loss on 15 June 2026, claimed on` (YMD 2026 7 1) `, settlement notice received` NOTHING `, dispute arising` NOTHING) BECAUSE "the record does not say when the dispute arose"
#ASSERT count `9.4 — the fora, in order` EQUALS 3
